cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VLC-1: Verifiable Completeness for AI System Logs"
message: "If you reference this specification, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Moore
    given-names: Matthew
    email: moorematthew131@gmail.com
version: "1.0-draft"
date-released: 2026-09-12
abstract: >-
  A vendor-neutral specification and conformance scheme for demonstrating the
  completeness of logs produced by AI systems. Defines five cumulative levels —
  tamper-evident, loss-accounted, coverage-declared, policy-bound and
  independently witnessed — with a machine-checked proof that the levels are
  strictly ordered and that each admits an attack the next refuses. Includes an
  adapter-driven conformance checker, worked example logs at every level, and a
  reconciler for checking an agent's self-reported transcript against an
  independent record.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - audit logging
  - log completeness
  - EU AI Act
  - prEN 18229
  - ISO/IEC 24970
  - formal verification
license: MIT
